## Cross-artifact rules

- Review only artifacts that may actually be affected; review does not imply that every related file must be edited.
- A change to the central question, candidate ranking, or stop condition requires review of the applicable entries in `RESEARCH_PLAN.md`, `SCIENTIFIC_PROGRESS.md`, and the matching packet.
- A change to include structure, section responsibilities, or claim status requires review of the affected parts of `{{CONTEXT_FILE}}` and `manuscript-project.toml`.
- A change to conventions, units, fields, boundary data, likelihood semantics, or canonical notation requires review of the affected profile guidance, derivations, configuration, code inputs, and TeX.
- An established numerical claim requires a fresh-input verifier for the named object; a plot, cached array, or successful smoke test is insufficient.
- A new citation requires review of `CITATION_PLAN.md`; a new generated figure or table requires its source, declared outputs, input route, and verification boundary.

